  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Six British Council Country evaluations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Looking at One-British Council in microcosm and generating evidence of our USP,namely how our different programmes add up to something greater than the sum of theindividual parts.2. How our networks, relationships and reservoir of expertise build up over many years,alongside our trusted brand and visible presence, making us the organisation of choice forindividuals, institutions and Governments.3. How we can broker and leverage more due to our connections, history and longevity.Showcasing the added value we can generate when additional money is invested into aCountry.The primary purpose of Country evaluations is an external business development and stakeholderengagement exercise. This will largely be at the Regional level, with existing and prospective partnersand stakeholders as the key target audience. However, evidence generated will also be valuable forcommunication centrally with UK Government, partners and key stakeholders, particularly thinkingahead to the Comprehensive Spending Review and new strategic partnerships work. There is animportant internal learning element too, though this is secondary. The other purpose of the Country evaluations is to establish new data collection systems now, particularly areas around brokering, connections and networks. This will help to automate the processof generating this evidence in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
